    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "First we draw a sketch and assign a coordinate system to the problem Figure 3.13. This is a simple problem, but it always helps to visualize it. Notice that we assign east as positive and west as negative. Thus, in this case, we have negative velocity."
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "text": "FIGURE 3.13 Identify the coordinate system, the given information, and what you want to determine. — A sketch showing a horizontal axis with a green dot representing initial velocity $v_o = 0$ at an origin, and another green dot representing final velocity $v_f = -15.0\\text{ m/s}$ with a green vector pointing left. An acceleration vector $a = ?$ points left below. On the right, a compass rose shows directions $N (+y)$, $S (-y)$, $E (+x)$, and $W (-x)$.",
