      "text": "FIGURE 3.15 (a, b) The velocity-versus-time graph is linear and has a negative constant slope (a) that is equal to acceleration, shown in (b). — Two graphs. Graph (a) shows $v(t) \\text{ (m/s)}$ versus Time (s) with a linear downward slope from $(0, 3)$ to $(1.5, -6)$. Graph (b) shows $a(t) \\text{ (m/s}^2\\text{)}$ versus Time (s) with a constant horizontal line at $a(t) = -6 \\text{ m/s}^2$ from $t = 0$ to $1.5\\text{ s}$.",
