        792,
        857
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "If we know the functional form of velocity, $v(t)$, we can calculate instantaneous acceleration $a(t)$ at any time point in the motion using Equation 3.9."
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "text": "EXAMPLE 3.6\n\nCalculating Instantaneous Acceleration\n\nA particle is in motion and is accelerating. The functional form of the velocity is $v(t) = (20 \\text{ m/s}^2)t - (5 \\text{ m/s}^3)t^2$.\n\na. Find the functional form of the acceleration."
