      "text": "The acceleration function is linear in time so the integration involves simple polynomials. In Figure 3.30, we see that if we extend the solution beyond the point when the velocity is zero, the velocity becomes negative and the boat reverses direction. This tells us that solutions can give us information outside our immediate interest and we should be careful when interpreting them."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "CHECK YOUR UNDERSTANDING 3.8"
    },
